1
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:34,800
Who wants to cook Aloo Gobi when you can bend a ball like Beckham?

2
00:08:57,600 --> 00:09:03,600
Bend It Like Beckham is a comedy, drama, romance
film directed by Gurinder Chadha.

3
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:32,400
Jess Bhamra, the daughter of a strict Indian couple in London, is not
permitted to play organized soccer, even though she is 18.

4
00:17:55,200 --> 00:18:01,200
When Jess is playing for fun one day, her impressive skills are seen by Jules
Paxton, who then convinces Jess to play for her semi-pro team.

5
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:30,000
Jess uses elaborate excuses to hide her matches from her family while
also dealing with her romantic feelings for her coach, Joe.

6
00:26:52,800 --> 00:26:58,800
Jesminder 'Jess' Kaur Bhamra, played by Parminder Nagra.

7
00:31:21,600 --> 00:31:27,600
Juliette 'Jules' Paxton, played by Keira Knightley.

8
00:35:50,400 --> 00:35:56,400
Joe, played by Jonathan Rhys Meyers.

9
00:40:19,200 --> 00:40:25,200
Mr. Bhamra, played by Anupam Kher.

10
00:44:48,000 --> 00:44:54,000
Mrs. Bhamra, played by Shaheen Khan.

11
00:49:16,800 --> 00:49:22,800
Pinky Bhamra, played by Archie Panjabi.

12
00:53:45,600 --> 00:53:51,600
Bend It Like Beckham is a 2002 sports comedy-drama film directed by Gurinder Chadha
from a screenplay by Chadha, Paul Mayeda Berges, and Guljit Bindra.

13
00:58:14,400 --> 00:58:20,400
The film stars Parminder Nagra, Keira Knightley, Jonathan Rhys Meyers, Anupam
Kher, Juliet Stevenson, Shaznay Lewis, and Archie Panjabi.

14
01:02:43,200 --> 01:02:49,200
In Bend It Like Beckham, Jesminder Bhamra (Nagra) and Jules Paxton (Knightley)
chase careers in professional football despite their parents' wishes.

15
01:07:12,000 --> 01:07:18,000
Development for the film began after Chadha, Bindra, and
Berges completed the screenplay by early 2001.

16
01:11:40,800 --> 01:11:46,800
Nagra and Knightley were hired soon after, with casting rounded out with the
additions of Meyers, Kher, Stevenson, Lewis, and Panjabi by that May.

17
01:16:09,600 --> 01:16:15,600
Principal photography began in June 2001 and lasted until September, with
filming locations including London, Shepperton Studios, and Hamburg.

18
01:20:38,400 --> 01:20:44,400
Production collaborated with The Football Association, while the film's title refers
to David Beckham's curling free kick technique, also known as bending.

19
01:25:07,199 --> 01:25:13,199
Bend It Like Beckham was theatrically released first in the
United Kingdom on 12 April 2002 by Helkon SK.

20
01:29:36,000 --> 01:29:42,000
The film surprised critics, who praised the screenplay, light-hearted
tone, and commentary on Punjabi social norms and culture.

21
01:34:04,800 --> 01:34:10,800
Bend It Like Beckham grossed $76.6 million at the box office.

22
01:38:33,600 --> 01:38:39,600
In 2015 it was adapted into a stage musical that opened at the Phoenix Theatre.

23
01:43:02,400 --> 01:43:08,400
The film explores themes of london, england, sports,
tradition, culture clash, immigration.

24
01:47:31,200 --> 01:47:37,200
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
